    "result_text": "Done. **BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, including the new `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` acceptance test.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `sharesHousehold` flag was already handled end-to-end (`RejectDuplicateHousehold` skips the duplicate-address check when it's true). What was missing was the `householdId` field. I added it as a **deterministically derived, read-only response field** rather than a persisted column:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` response schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it), documented as \"shared by every owner with the same last name and address.\"\n\n2. **`HouseholdId.java`** (new helper in `rest.function.owner`) \u2014 `HouseholdId.of(lastName, address)` normalizes last name + address the *same way* as `RejectDuplicateHousehold` (trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case) and returns the first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over the pair.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that fills `householdId` from the owner's last name and address, mirroring how `displayName`/`initials` are derived.\n\n## Why this design\n\nBecause `householdId` is a pure function of `lastName` + `address`, any two owners in the same household (matching last name and address \u2014 exactly the owners `sharesHousehold: true` permits) compute the *identical, stable* id automatically, with no cross-owner lookup or mutation of existing rows. That satisfies \"assign both the same householdId (a stable shared identifier)\" while avoiding a schema migration, entity field, `data.sql` seed edits, and a new pipeline step \u2014 a smaller, lower-risk change than persisting the column (following the pattern of `displayName`/`initials`, not `customerCode` which needs persistence because it uses a global sequence).\n\nThe test creates owner `a`, then `b` and `c` with `a`'s last name/address and `sharesHousehold: true`; it asserts `b` and `c` return equal, non-blank `householdId` values via `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 which now holds.",
